// What a vehicle of examples/parking believes (check/belief.ent;
// parking-SPEC.md, check 4): it drives up to 30 cm from a low wall,
// where none of its cameras sees the wall any more, and the grid still
// holds it. Without errors the believed pose is the true one to the bit
// and the distance read off the grid within a centimetre of the true
// one; with errors the pose is off by centimetres after 2.7 m and the
// reading by some more. On one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/belief.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/belief.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// CHECK: errors false: pose off 0 um 0 urad exact true, true 3000 reads 1000000 {{.*}} seen low 11, cells 0
// CHECK: errors false: pose off 0 um 0 urad exact true, true 285 reads 294 (off by 9), seen low 0, cells 152
// CHECK: errors true: pose off 0 um 0 urad exact true, true 3000
// Less than 1.5 percent of 2.7 m (40 mm), and the reading within 15 cm.
// CHECK: errors true: pose off {{[1-3][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} um {{[0-9]+}} urad exact false, true 285 reads {{[1-4][0-9][0-9]}} (off by {{[0-9][0-9]?}}), seen low 0
